1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,441
Mempire is for crypto-native players who want

2
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:05,720
real stakes without wallet friction.

3
00:00:06,167 --> 00:00:07,668
Every coin is a fighter,

4
00:00:07,688 --> 00:00:09,711
and the market decides who is strong

5
00:00:09,731 --> 00:00:10,492
today.

6
00:00:10,753 --> 00:00:12,288
This is the live app,

7
00:00:12,308 --> 00:00:14,207
on Monad testnet.

8
00:00:14,807 --> 00:00:17,039
Sign-up is one passkey prompt,

9
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:18,134
through Mera.

10
00:00:18,394 --> 00:00:20,676
No seed phrase, no extension.

11
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:23,576
The relayer mints an eight-card starter deck,

12
00:00:23,596 --> 00:00:26,536
sends test AUSD from Agora's faucet,

13
00:00:26,556 --> 00:00:28,478
and a little MON for gas.

14
00:00:29,078 --> 00:00:30,895
That strip is Monad itself:

15
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:32,936
each block voted in about three hundred

16
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:36,340
milliseconds, and final in under six hundred.

17
00:00:39,745 --> 00:00:41,675
Minting a new fighter pulls a live

18
00:00:41,695 --> 00:00:43,823
Pyth price into the same transaction,

19
00:00:43,843 --> 00:00:45,472
and the card records the price it

20
00:00:45,492 --> 00:00:46,682
was minted at.

21
00:00:49,745 --> 00:00:51,989
The market meta, written on chain by

22
00:00:52,009 --> 00:00:54,752
a Chainlink workflow, buffs and nerfs each

23
00:00:54,772 --> 00:00:55,545
fighter.

24
00:00:55,898 --> 00:00:58,525
We stake the one-dollar tier in MON,

25
00:00:58,545 --> 00:01:00,305
and queue a ranked match.

26
00:01:05,995 --> 00:01:07,554
Every card I drop is its own

27
00:01:07,574 --> 00:01:10,236
Monad transaction, from a per-match session key,

28
00:01:10,256 --> 00:01:11,748
so there are no popups.

29
00:01:12,102 --> 00:01:14,372
Each pill is a real round trip:

30
00:01:14,563 --> 00:01:16,694
executed, then final.

31
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:19,963
We fast-forward the middle of the match.

32
00:01:20,096 --> 00:01:21,589
And a tower falls.

33
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:45,208
The second player's claim settles the pot

34
00:01:45,228 --> 00:01:46,081
on chain:

35
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,901
ninety percent to the winner,

36
00:01:47,921 --> 00:01:49,062
ten to the house,

37
00:01:49,082 --> 00:01:50,307
plus a chest.

38
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:57,160
Clans and clan wars score only the

39
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:59,471
staked wins the relay has verified on

40
00:01:59,491 --> 00:02:00,240
chain.

41
00:02:00,501 --> 00:02:02,489
These clans were seeded by our team

42
00:02:02,509 --> 00:02:03,537
for the demo.

43
00:02:03,984 --> 00:02:06,100
Joining one puts us straight into its

44
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:06,962
war.

45
00:02:11,536 --> 00:02:13,176
Empire holds the leaderboard,

46
00:02:13,196 --> 00:02:16,148
Monad's native staking precompile read live,

47
00:02:16,168 --> 00:02:18,575
and a passkey signature verified by Monad's

48
00:02:18,595 --> 00:02:20,981
P-256 precompile.

49
00:02:30,703 --> 00:02:32,575
And the proof, read live from the

50
00:02:32,595 --> 00:02:33,263
chain:

51
00:02:33,617 --> 00:02:36,163
the Chainlink report, a Pyth-priced mint,

52
00:02:36,183 --> 00:02:37,687
and a gasless chest,

53
00:02:37,715 --> 00:02:41,913
opened through EIP-7702 and our own paymaster.

54
00:02:42,513 --> 00:02:43,399
Mempire.

55
00:02:43,419 --> 00:02:44,853
Every coin is a fighter.

56
00:02:44,928 --> 00:02:46,719
Play it now, at mempire monad,

57
00:02:46,739 --> 00:02:48,522
dot vercel, dot app.
